The bot should be able to ban users from a specific guild (server) using the ban command. The command should take two arguments: the user ID of the user to be banned, and a reason for the ban. The bot should then use the Discord API to ban the user from the guild. The bot should also send a message to the channel where the ban command was used, indicating that the user has been banned and providing the reason for the ban.

Here is some sample code to get you started:

```javascript
const { Client, GatewayIntentBits, Events } = require('discord.js');
const { token } = require('./config.json');

// Create a new Discord client
const client = new Client({ intents: [GatewayIntentBits.Guilds] });

// Event listener for when the client is ready
client.on(Events.ClientReady, () => {
  console.log('Bot is ready!');
});

// Event listener for when a message is sent
client.on(Events.MessageCreate, async (message) => {
  // Check if the message contains the command prefix and the command name
  if (!message.content.startsWith('!') || message.author.bot) return;

  const args = message.content.slice(1).split(' ');
  const command = args.shift().toLowerCase();

  // Check if the command is "ban"
  if (command === 'ban') {
    // Check if there are enough arguments
    if (args.length < 2) {
      return message.reply('Please provide a user ID and a reason for the ban.');
    }

    // Get the user ID and reason from the arguments
    const userId = args[0];
    const reason = args.slice(1).join(' ');

    try {
      // Ban the user from the guild
      await message.guild.members.ban(userId, { reason });

      // Send a message indicating that the user has been banned
      await message.channel.send(`User ${userId} has been banned. Reason: ${reason}`);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
      return message.reply('There was an error while banning the user.');
    }
  }
});

// Login to Discord with the bot token
client.login(token);
```
