• If n is less than or equal to 1, return n since there is only one possible Fibonacci number for those values.
• Calculate the current Fibonacci number by adding together the previous two Fibonacci numbers.
• Update the previous two Fibonacci numbers with the current and previous values.
• Repeat steps 2 and 3 until we reach the desired nth Fibonacci number.

